# The ledger's configuration. Every variable the service reads is declared in src/env.ts and
# appears here; nothing else is passed to the container (rule 9 of docs/ecosystem/03 §2).

PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=production
LOG_LEVEL=info
CLOUDSFORGE_TAG=dev

# Rule 1: one database, named by this service's own variable. The ledger shares a database with
# nothing — AD-06 and AD-17 put it on the `vault` network with custody and settlement.
LEDGER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://cloudsforge:CHANGE_ME@postgres:5432/ledger
LEDGER_DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# Service tokens are RS256, issued by identity, and carry `ledger:post`, `ledger:read` and
# `ledger:reserve`. The shared PAY_SERVICE_TOKEN is retired — AD-17.
IDENTITY_JWKS_URL=http://identity:4000/.well-known/jwks.json
IDENTITY_ISSUER=https://identity.cloudsforge.online

# HMAC key for outbound event signatures. Run `openssl rand -base64 48`. The boot guard
# checks the SHAPE — base64 or hex, 32 decoded bytes, a measured entropy floor — so a typed
# value is refused however long it is, and there is no NODE_ENV exemption (micro-org #142).
OUTBOX_SIGNING_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_run_openssl_rand_base64_48

# Reconciliation. Per-asset drift tolerance in SMALLEST UNITS, as a JSON object of strings.
#
# An asset absent from this map gets ZERO tolerance, not unlimited — `withinTolerance` in
# contracts-money fails closed, and that is deliberate: an asset silently exempt from the only
# check that guards it is worse than an asset that alerts too often. The example below allows
# 0.001 EMBER (18 decimals) of fees in flight.
#
# LTC IS STATED AT ZERO ON PURPOSE, and it is not the same thing as leaving it out — the behaviour
# is identical, the readability is not. Litecoin is a UTXO chain of 8 decimals: the indexer sums
# integer outputs, this ledger sums integer postings, neither side rounds, so there is no scale gap
# for a tolerance to absorb and any drift at all is real. A one-satoshi drift therefore freezes LTC
# withdrawals, which is the correct answer for a custodian that cannot account for a unit of
# somebody's money. BTC, ETH, SOL and XRP are at zero by the same argument, by absence; LTC is
# written out because an absence cannot tell "decided" apart from "forgotten".
LEDGER_ASSET_TOLERANCE={"EMBER":"1000000000000000","LTC":"0"}
# WHICH assets are swept, which is NOT the same list as which assets are chain-settled. LTC is
# absent here for the same reason BTC, ETH, SOL and XRP are: nothing indexes them for this estate
# yet, and this default is not an enumeration of ON_CHAIN_ASSETS. Adding an asset here without a
# feed freezes its withdrawals — see the EMBER argument in src/env.ts, which is the worked example.
LEDGER_RECONCILE_ASSETS=SHARD,EMBER
LEDGER_RECONCILE_NETWORK=testnet

# The chain half of the solvency invariant: GET /v1/custody/:chain/:network/total on micro-indexer.
#
# OPTIONAL, AND UNSET IS NOT A DISABLED CHECK — IT IS A FAILING ONE. Without a URL no chain asset
# can be observed, so every ON_CHAIN_ASSETS member records `unavailable`/`failed` and freezes
# withdrawals. It is optional only because src/migrator.ts shares this env module and the migrate
# container is given no indexer; demanding one would kill it and take the estate's schema with it.
# The service logs a fatal line at boot naming the assets it is about to freeze.
INDEXER_URL=http://indexer:4000

# Absolute ceiling on that call, across connect and body. It bounds a JOB'S LEASE as much as a
# request: the reconciliation handler holds its lease for the whole call, so a provider holding the
# socket open blocks the asset's next sweep. Integer 100–60000.
LEDGER_INDEXER_DEADLINE_MS=5000

# THE LONG-LIVED CREDENTIAL THIS SERVICE EXCHANGES FOR THE TOKENS IT PRESENTS TO THE INDEXER.
#
# It REPLACES `LEDGER_SERVICE_TOKEN`, and the replacement is the point. That variable held a
# 600-second token read once at import (identity/src/tokens.ts:28) and the reconciliation job runs
# every 900 seconds (src/jobs.ts) — so the chain-backing call authenticated once per bootstrap and
# never again. Every sweep after minute ten got a 401, mapped it to no observation, and froze EMBER
# while writing BYTE-IDENTICAL rows, logs and events to the honest "the chain could not be observed"
# freeze. The guarantee reported a true-shaped fact for a false reason and nobody could tell.
#
# A credential is not a token: it confers nothing by itself, it is revocable, it survives a restart,
# and @cloudsforge/auth's ServiceTokenProvider exchanges it at POST /service-tokens/exchange for an
# ordinary ten-minute token, re-minting at ~80% of its life. The ten minutes is UNCHANGED — rotation
# IS expiry, and lengthening the TTL would leave the same defect arriving later and hurting more.
#
# Mint one with POST /service-credentials on micro-identity; `deploy/scripts/estate-bootstrap.sh`
# already writes `LEDGER_IDENTITY_CREDENTIAL` into its tokens file. It begins `cfsc_`, and a
# container handed a JWT here fails at construction rather than ten minutes later.
#
# UNSET IS A SUPPORTED MODE and it fails closed — and, since migration 12, LEGIBLY: the call is
# never sent unauthenticated, and the run records `unavailable` with
# `unobserved_reason = 'no_credential'` rather than the row an unfollowed chain writes. It must stay
# optional because src/migrator.ts shares this env module and `ledger-migrate` is given no identity
# credential; demanding it would kill the container the estate's schema waits on.
#
# Left empty here on purpose rather than given a placeholder: a placeholder that boots is how a
# secret from a repository reaches production. The GRANT is DERIVED from `INDEXER_SCOPES` in
# src/indexerclient.ts by deploy/scripts/derive-grants.mjs; a grant added by hand to the compose
# file fails that check.
LEDGER_IDENTITY_CREDENTIAL=

# Where identity is, for POST /service-tokens/exchange. Defaults to IDENTITY_ISSUER, which is
# already required and is identity's own base URL — the issuer of a token is by definition where the
# token came from. Set it only where the two genuinely differ (an issuer behind a public name,
# dialled internally); pointing the exchange at one identity and the JWKS at another fails with a
# signature error nobody reads as a configuration mistake.
# IDENTITY_URL=http://identity:4000

# RETIRED. `LEDGER_SERVICE_TOKEN` is read for exactly one purpose — to log an ERROR at boot saying
# it is set and is IGNORED. An operator who redeploys with the old variable and not the new one
# would otherwise get a service that looks configured and is not, which is a quieter version of the
# defect the credential replaced. Remove it from your deploy rather than setting it here.
# LEDGER_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# How long an idempotency key is honoured. Expiring one EARLY means the next replay of it does the
# work a second time, so this must outlive every caller's retry horizon.
LEDGER_IDEMPOTENCY_TTL_DAYS=30

# Names this replica in jobs.locked_by. Defaults to the hostname, which is the container id under
# compose and the pod name under Kubernetes.
# INSTANCE_ID=

# Database tests run only against a database whose name contains "test", because they truncate.
# Unset, every database test skips.
# LEDGER_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://cloudsforge:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/ledger_test
